{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3XWGf3Ppxiwk2EMixj1Yu","type":"tool_result","content":"450\t      \"Understand the three main Singapore work pass types for Malaysians: Employment Pass, S Pass, and Work Permit. Compare salary minimums, eligibility, and which visa suits your career stage.\",\n451\t    date: \"2026-04-14\",\n452\t    category: \"Career & Work\",\n453\t    author: \"Jay Lew\",\n454\t    readTime: \"12 min read\",\n455\t    tags: [\"singapore\", \"work-pass\", \"career\", \"expat\", \"malaysia\", \"employment-pass\", \"visa\"],\n456\t    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/singapore-work-pass-guide.jpg\",\n457\t    content: `\n458\t<h2>Singapore's Work Visa System Explained</h2>\n459\t<p>Malaysia is Singapore's top source of migrant workers, accounting for 30% of foreign labour. The Ministry of Manpower (MOM) manages work passes under three main categories: Employment Pass (EP), S Pass, and Work Permit. Each serves a different skill level and salary band. Understanding which pass you qualify for is critical before job hunting.</p>\n460\t\n461\t<h2>Quick Comparison: EP vs S Pass vs Work Permit</h2>\n462\t<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%; margin:16px 0; border-collapse:collapse;\">\n463\t<tr style=\"background:#f5f5f5;\">\n464\t<th><strong>Feature</strong></th>\n465\t<th><strong>Employment Pass (EP)</strong></th>\n466\t<th><strong>S Pass</strong></th>\n467\t<th><strong>Work Permit</strong></th>\n468\t</tr>\n469\t<tr>\n470\t<td><strong>Minimum Salary</strong></td>\n471\t<td>SGD 5,000/month</td>\n472\t<td>SGD 3,150/month</td>\n473\t<td>No fixed minimum</td>\n474\t</tr>\n475\t<tr>\n476\t<td><strong>Target Profile</strong></td>\n477\t<td>Degree-holders, senior roles</td>\n478\t<td>Diploma or 5yrs experience</td>\n479\t<td>Semi-skilled, unskilled labour</td>\n480\t</tr>\n481\t<tr>\n482\t<td><strong>Processing Time</strong></td>\n483\t<td>1-4 weeks</td>\n484\t<td>2-8 weeks</td>\n485\t<td>1-2 weeks</td>\n486\t</tr>\n487\t<tr>\n488\t<td><strong>Validity</strong></td>\n489\t<td>Up to 3 years</td>\n490\t<td>Up to 2 years</td>\n491\t<td>Up to 2 years</td>\n492\t</tr>\n493\t<tr>\n494\t<td><strong>Family Dependents</strong></td>\n495\t<td>Yes (spouse + kids)</td>\n496\t<td>Limited (with approval)</td>\n497\t<td>No</td>\n498\t</tr>\n499\t<tr>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6da17fb6-3289-4255-a288-226ac7439267","uuid":"d477e1de-2b27-492e-9417-5204bd95dd44","timestamp":"2026-04-14T09:33:00.919Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts","content":"      \"Understand the three main Singapore work pass types for Malaysians: Employment Pass, S Pass, and Work Permit. Compare salary minimums, eligibility, and which visa suits your career stage.\",\n    date: \"2026-04-14\",\n    category: \"Career & Work\",\n    author: \"Jay Lew\",\n    readTime: \"12 min read\",\n    tags: [\"singapore\", \"work-pass\", \"career\", \"expat\", \"malaysia\", \"employment-pass\", \"visa\"],\n    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/singapore-work-pass-guide.jpg\",\n    content: `\n<h2>Singapore's Work Visa System Explained</h2>\n<p>Malaysia is Singapore's top source of migrant workers, accounting for 30% of foreign labour. The Ministry of Manpower (MOM) manages work passes under three main categories: Employment Pass (EP), S Pass, and Work Permit. Each serves a different skill level and salary band. Understanding which pass you qualify for is critical before job hunting.</p>\n\n<h2>Quick Comparison: EP vs S Pass vs Work Permit</h2>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%; margin:16px 0; border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#f5f5f5;\">\n<th><strong>Feature</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Employment Pass (EP)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>S Pass</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Work Permit</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Minimum Salary</strong></td>\n<td>SGD 5,000/month</td>\n<td>SGD 3,150/month</td>\n<td>No fixed minimum</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Target Profile</strong></td>\n<td>Degree-holders, senior roles</td>\n<td>Diploma or 5yrs experience</td>\n<td>Semi-skilled, unskilled labour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Processing Time</strong></td>\n<td>1-4 weeks</td>\n<td>2-8 weeks</td>\n<td>1-2 weeks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Validity</strong></td>\n<td>Up to 3 years</td>\n<td>Up to 2 years</td>\n<td>Up to 2 years</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Family Dependents</strong></td>\n<td>Yes (spouse + kids)</td>\n<td>Limited (with approval)</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>","numLines":50,"startLine":450,"totalLines":1100}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VkfYTT232XoiDL76mjZh43","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that:\n1. Blog posts are defined as objects in a `rawPosts` array\n2. Each post has: slug, title, excerpt, date, category, author, readTime, tags, featuredImage, and content\n3. Content is HTML\n4. There are tables that use HTML table syntax with border, cellpadding, cellspacing, and inline styles\n5. The file has computed reading time\n\nNow let me look at the end of the file to see where the rawPosts array ends and the export statement.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":76678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6da17fb6-3289-4255-a288-226ac7439267","uuid":"03fbcd21-d382-4f62-8bb6-570ffa119925"}
